  </table>

  <p>Even in bear-regime periods, forward returns remain positive — gold's long-term drift dominates short-term momentum signals. The crossover adds marginal value in timing entry points but is not a reliable short signal.</p>

  <h3>Volume & Liquidity Profile</h3>
  <p>Volume data in the early years (2000–2003) is sparse and unreliable (frequent zero-volume days). Post-2004, volume stabilizes with a weak negative correlation to absolute returns (r = –0.025), suggesting that higher volume does not systematically coincide with larger price moves in gold — unlike equity markets where volume typically confirms volatility.</p>

